xt":"Each record keeps what the body holds of it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":";","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its "},{"code":"EventRecord\/timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", to the millisecond the body holds;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its event, a value of the decoder’s type of that "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", read through the type’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", its "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values included;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the context the body’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"},{"type":"text","text":" holds: the session’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", the sample rate, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context keys, and the trace context, which the decoder’s instrument extracts."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record has no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/sourceLocation"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/deliveryTag"},{"text":", which the body","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t hold, and it reveals its sensitive values, as a tracked record does, so a destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"text":" still redacts them. Encoding the records again with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" of the same plan, and an instrument that injects what it extracts,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the same bytes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body names each record’s event but not its version, so a record is read at the version of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the decoder’s type of that name, and the plan must hold a schema of that version. Deploy the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decoder with the event types the apps send. Once a type’s version is raised, a record an older"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app sends at the earlier version is read as the newer one: it is reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError\/undecodableProperty(event:property:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when its properties don’t fit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the newer type, and read as the newer version when they do."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the decoder can’t read is left out and the batch’s other records are read: one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event it has no type of, one whose type’s version the plan has no schema of, a member that is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"missing or holds what the encoder never writes, and a property the event’s type can’t read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder\/batch(from:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns each as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/UndecodedRecord","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property a delivery redacted is missing, so its record reads back only when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property is optional or has a default value; a redacted "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" element of an array is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", so a record whose array of non-optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" elements was redacted is reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError\/undecodableProperty(event:property:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". An integer outside its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property’s type, such as 300 for a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt8"},{"type":"text","text":", is reported the same way. A property of a type the plan can’t map reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"back only as far as its JSON holds what its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decodable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance reads: a whole "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside it is written without a fraction, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":" inside it as a timestamp, neither of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which it reads."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A body that isn’t a collector batch at all throws ","type":"text"},{"identifie